{"title":"Career Roadmap · GIS Analyst","role":"GIS Analyst","summary":"A GIS Analyst works with geospatial data to understand locations, patterns, relationships, and changes across physical and human environments.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E.","Course":"Geoinformatics / Geomatics Engineering"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A GIS Analyst works with geospatial data to understand locations, patterns, relationships, and changes across physical and human environments."},{"type":"p","text":"For a Geoinformatics/Geomatics Engineering graduate, the career combines:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Geographic Information Systems (GIS)"},{"text":"Remote sensing"},{"text":"Surveying"},{"text":"Cartography"},{"text":"Spatial databases"},{"text":"GNSS/GPS"},{"text":"Geospatial analytics"},{"text":"Satellite imagery"},{"text":"Python programming"},{"text":"Spatial statistics"},{"text":"Web GIS"},{"text":"3D geospatial technologies"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The role can be applied across urban planning, infrastructure, utilities, agriculture, environmental management, disaster management, transportation, telecommunications, defense, logistics, and location intelligence."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"note","label":"2026–2030","text":"GIS & Geospatial Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Build practical skills in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"GIS software"},{"text":"Spatial data creation"},{"text":"Map production"},{"text":"Coordinate systems"},{"text":"Georeferencing"},{"text":"Digitization"},{"text":"Spatial queries"},{"text":"Remote sensing fundamentals"},{"text":"GNSS/GPS"},{"text":"Basic Python"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential entry-level roles:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"GIS Analyst"},{"text":"GIS Executive"},{"text":"GIS Technician"},{"text":"Junior GIS Analyst"},{"text":"Geospatial Analyst"},{"text":"Mapping Analyst"},{"